    [BugFix][PCP] Support multimodal inputs for DeepSeek V4.1 (#18281)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Enable MRV2 PCP multimodal inputs for DeepSeek V4.1. Use the batch's
    common padded length for embedding all-gather and reduce-scatter when
    ranks have unequal valid token counts, while reusing fixed-capacity
    buffers and returning only local valid rows. Fine-grained DP embedding
    exchange retains its fixed-capacity behavior.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. MRV2 PCP accepts multimodal inputs.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Local CPU validation at `c795e27b7`: **38 tests passed**; `./format.sh
    ci` passed. Covers PCP/TP exchange, unequal token counts, batch
    transitions, idle ranks, stable buffer addresses, and the MRV2
    multimodal preparation path.
    
    A3, 16 NPUs, TP1. MMMU validation: fixed first 100 questions,
    concurrency 64, three rounds per configuration. Engram ON, DSpark5,
    `FULL_DECODE_ONLY`, temperature=0, seed=1024, `enable_thinking=False`,
    max output tokens=16384.
    
    | Configuration | Correct / 100, three rounds | Median accuracy |
    |---|---|---:|
    | PCP1 / DP16 / EP16 | 74 / 77 / 72 | 74.00% |
    | PCP8 / DP2 / EP16 | 73 / 74 / 75 | 74.00% |
    
    PCP minus DP: **0.00 percentage points**. All 600 requests completed
    successfully. Output-limit finishes: DP 28, PCP 27; truncated and
    unparsed answers remain in the scoring denominator.
    
    MMMU accuracy commit (before the common-span optimization): `dd961f84c`;
    vLLM: `ced6857a`.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
